The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
static const struct vm_operations_struct uacce_vm_ops = {
	.close = uacce_vma_close,
};
```
Reason: Missing the .mremap callback allows the default mremap behavior, which copies vm_private_data (i.e., the queue pointer q) to the new VMA. When both the original and new VMAs are unmapped via munmap, uacce_vma_close is invoked twice on the same q, causing a double-free of q->qfr.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
static int uacce_vma_mremap(struct vm_area_struct *area)
{
	return -EPERM;
}

static const struct vm_operations_struct uacce_vm_ops = {
	.close = uacce_vma_close,
	.mremap = uacce_vma_mremap,
};
```
Reason: Implementing .mremap to return -EPERM explicitly forbids mremap operations. This prevents the creation of a second VMA that shares the same vm_private_data, thereby ensuring that uacce_vma_close is called only once on the queue pointer and eliminating the double-free risk.

